Uncommitted FEX changes on 2026-10-11, saved so they aren't lost; not part of the build's patch series.
Downstream only: written with Claude for MacNeutron, never for submission to FEX (FEX takes no AI-written code).
Base: the FEX tree with wine-arm64/patches/fex 0001-0010 applied (commit b71e03d in build/wine-arm64-src/fex).
Apply with: git -C build/wine-arm64-src/fex apply aoe2/wip/fex-uncommitted-20261011.patch
- Pool buffers: code from non-file-backed memory compiles into separate, recycled buffers (MACNEUTRON_POOL_BUFFER_MB),
  plus MACNEUTRON_CODE_BUFFER_MB; test in wine-arm64/tests/x64-poolchurn.c (HANDOFF §4 item 2).
- No deadlock when VirtualDontNeed frees the call-ret stack under the code invalidation lock (memset instead,
  FEXCore::Allocator::SuppressMemoryNotifications).

