+/**
+ * MacNeutron (downstream only, not for upstream FEX): code buffers for code compiled from memory that isn't
+ * file-backed.
+ *
+ * Anti-tamper code that keeps writing new arrangements of relocated instructions into private memory (Age of Empires
+ * II: Definitive Edition, ~10 MB of new host code a second) fills the shared code buffer every few seconds, and each
+ * refill makes every thread recompile its working set. Such code goes to pool buffers of a fixed size instead, so it
+ * no longer fills the main one. A full pool buffer is replaced by a new one; threads move to it at their next
+ * compile, as they do between main buffers, and an old one lives while a thread still holds it. Blocks are never
+ * linked between a pool buffer and a main one, so no code outside a pool buffer can jump into one a thread no
+ * longer holds.
+ */
+class PoolCodeBuffers {
+public:
+  explicit PoolCodeBuffers(SharedCodeBufferManager& Registry);
+
+  bool Enabled() const {
+    return Size != 0;
+  }
+
